**Definition 4.1 (Boundary atoms and an invariant functional).** Let
$\mathcal K_\partial$ be the cone generated by real unit product
atoms $k(a,b)$ for which at least one of the two factors has zero
population in at least one of the sectors $0,+,-$. Define

$$
\Phi(M,\eta)=M_{00}+2M_{++}+2M_{--}
-\frac32(\eta_++\eta_-+\eta_\Delta+\eta_\Sigma).
\tag{4.1}
$$

The boundary condition refers to either independent factor. It
includes, but is larger than, the two-orbit support in
[QJM, Proposition 4.1](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_QUANTUM_JOINT_MARGINAL_AND_ATTAINING_PORT.md).

